Q: Add custom attribute of age in model A: <p>The format for adding mutators has changed since laravel 8.</p>
<p>In <a href="https://laravel.com/docs/11.x/eloquent-mutators#defining-an-accessor" rel="nofollow noreferrer">laravel 11</a> (your setup) your mutator needs to return an attribute class instance.</p>
<pre><code>use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Casts\Attribute;


protected function age(): Attribute
{
    return Attribute::make(
        get: fn () =&gt; $this-&gt;birthdate-&gt;diffInYears(\Carbon\Carbon::now()),
    );
}
</code></pre>
<p>Dont forget to cast your attribute &quot;birthdate&quot; as a date/datetime to use carbon methods directly</p>
<pre><code>protected function casts(): array
{
    return [
        'birthdate' =&gt; 'datetime:Y-m-d',
    ];
}
</code></pre>
